==English==
[[File:Monty Python Live 02-07-14 13 21 20 (14598720721).jpg|thumb|"Encore" message during the show ''Monty Python Live (Mostly)'' in 2014.]]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|fr|encore||more, again}}, and once used in this sense.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɒŋkɔː/|/ˈɒ̃kɔː/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɑnkɔɹ/|/ˈɑŋkɔɹ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-encore.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{hyphenation|en|en|core}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# {{lb|en|conjunctive|hapax}} In addition to what has been said; [[furthermore]]; [[additionally]].
#* {{RQ:Landon Romance|page=181|volume=II|passage='''Encore''', attachments thwarted by circumstance, or such as died the natural death of absence—these would be not a few; to say nothing of some half-dozen grand passions.}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A brief extra [[performance]], done after the main performance is complete.
#: {{ux|en|To play an '''encore'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|Can I get an '''encore'''? We want more!}}
# A call or demand (as by continued [[applause]]) for a repeat performance.
#: {{ux|en|The '''encores''' were numerous.}}

